# ansipath

#### A super simple tool to parse your bash `ENV $PATH` variable with ansi codes, to make it prettier and more readable.

Will alert you to duplicate and dead links, as well.

---

### Bonus: `pathmunge` function to safely add paths in your `.profile`, `.bash_profile`, `.zprofile`, etc.

Use it to add `$PATH` directories instead of `export PATH="/your/executables/bin:$PATH"` to avoid duplicates

---

#### Portability:

Since `ansipath` works without using any python libraries other than `os`, it should work across all platforms (bash, zsh, etc.) and on essentially any modern version of Python3.

#### Installation:

git clone https://github.com/averyfreeman/ansipath
cd ansipath
uv tool install .

#### OR add the one-liner to your .bashrc:

echo 'source "$(pwd)/ansipath_func.sh"' >> $HOME/.bashrc

(note: this version that ONLY colors your `$PATH`)
